 AI-Powered Intelligent Driver Assistance System (ADAS)


The AI-Powered Intelligent Driver Assistance System (ADAS) is a deep learning-based computer vision project designed to improve road safety by detecting lane markings, road objects, traffic signs, and potholes.

The project utilizes YOLO11 (You Only Look Once) for real-time detection and analysis of road environments.

The system consists of three independent modules:

1. Lane Detection
2. Object Detection and Traffic Sign Detection
3. Pothole Detection

 Project Objectives

* Detect road lane markings and boundaries.
* Identify vehicles and other objects on roads.
* Detect and classify traffic signs.
* Identify potholes and damaged road surfaces.
* Process road images and video streams.
* Visualize detection results using bounding boxes, labels, and lane markings.
* Support the development of intelligent road safety monitoring systems.

 Project Modules

1.  Lane Detection

Description

The Lane Detection module focuses on identifying road lane markings to assist drivers in understanding road boundaries and lane positioning.

Key Features

* Road lane identification.
* Left and right lane boundary detection.
* Lane marking visualization.
* Image and video processing.
* Real-time lane monitoring.

Working Principle

1. Capture road images or video frames.
2. Preprocess the input frames.
3. Process the frames using a suitable YOLO11 lane detection or segmentation model.
4. Identify lane markings.
5. Visualize detected lane boundaries.

Expected Output

Road images or video frames with highlighted lane markings.

⸻

2.  Object Detection and Traffic Sign Detection

Description

This module combines Object Detection and Traffic Sign Detection to identify road objects and important traffic signs.

It uses YOLO11 for real-time visual recognition.

A. Object Detection

Key Features:

* Vehicle detection.
* Car, bus, truck, and motorcycle identification.
* Road object classification.
* Bounding box visualization.
* Detection confidence scores.

Working Principle:

1. Capture the input frame.
2. Process the frame using YOLO11.
3. Detect objects present in the scene.
4. Generate bounding boxes.
5. Display detected object labels and confidence scores.

B. Traffic Sign Detection

Key Features:

* Traffic sign identification.
* Recognition of supported traffic sign categories.
* Traffic sign classification.
* Bounding box visualization.
* Real-time traffic sign monitoring.

Working Principle:

1. Capture road images or video frames.
2. Process the frames using a trained YOLO11 model.
3. Detect visible traffic signs.
4. Classify the detected signs.
5. Display detection results.

Expected Output

Annotated images or videos containing detected road objects, traffic signs, bounding boxes, and confidence scores.

⸻

3.  Pothole Detection

Description

The Pothole Detection module focuses on identifying potholes and damaged road surfaces using YOLO11.

Potholes can cause vehicle damage, accidents, and unsafe driving conditions. This module aims to detect visible potholes and improve road hazard awareness.

Key Features

* Pothole identification.
* Detection of visible road surface damage.
* Real-time road condition monitoring.
* Bounding box visualization.
* Confidence score display.
* Image and video-based pothole detection.

Working Principle

1. Capture road images or video frames.
2. Preprocess the input frames.
3. Pass the frames through a custom-trained YOLO11 pothole detection model.
4. Identify potholes in the road scene.
5. Generate bounding boxes around detected potholes.
6. Display pothole detection results.

Expected Output

Road images or video frames with detected potholes highlighted using bounding boxes and confidence scores.

